+* UAE - The Un*x Amiga Emulator
+*
+* Netplay: two emulators run the same Amiga in lockstep over TCP.
+*
+* Both machines start from the same power-on state (same configuration,
+* ROM, floppy images and random seed) and only input events travel over
+* the network. Input captured on frame N is applied on both machines at
+* frame N + delay, at the same emulated position (vpos 0), so emulation
+* stays identical. Memory/CPU checksums are exchanged to detect desync.
+*
+* The host owns Amiga joystick port 2 (player 1 in most games), the
+* client's joystick is moved to joystick port 1 (the mouse port).
+*
+*/
